Dear Seller,

Your shop (Shop ID: 884266, Shop Name: VigilyxTech) has been suspended
due to a violation of Shopee's Intellectual Property Policy. You have
48 hours to submit an appeal.

Suspension Details:
  Shop ID: 884266
  Shop Name: VigilyxTech
  Marketplace: Shopee Malaysia (MY)
  Violation: Intellectual Property Infringement
  Complaint Source: Apple Inc. (Case #IP-MY-2026-4471)
  Affected Listings: 12 SKUs (iPhone-compatible accessories)
  Appeal Deadline: 2026-10-22 09:45

Why was my shop suspended?
  On October 15, Apple Inc. filed a complaint alleging that 12 of your
  product listings use "iPhone" and "MFi-Certified" without authorization.

How to Appeal:
  Please navigate to the Seller Centre manually in your browser:

  1. Open seller.shopee.com.my (type the URL manually)
  2. Log in with your registered seller email and password
  3. Go to Shop Health → Suspension Appeals → Submit New Appeal
  4. Select appeal type (Authorization Appeal or Product Modification Appeal)
  5. Upload required documents

  Important Security Notes:
  Shopee will NEVER:
  - Send you a direct appeal link via email
  - Ask for bank account details through an email portal
  - Ask for your passport or national ID through email
  - Offer a "quick appeal channel" that bypasses login

  All appeal actions must be done within the Seller Centre after you
  manually navigate to seller.shopee.com.my.

Required Appeal Documents:
  1. Brand Authorization Letter (or proof of product modification)
  2. Supplier Invoices for affected SKUs
  3. Business License

Consequences of Permanent Suspension:
  - All 847 listings permanently removed
  - Settlement funds (~MYR 42,300) frozen for 180 days
  - Seller account permanently banned
  - Related accounts also suspended

Settlement Fund Release:
  Frozen funds are visible in Seller Centre → Finance → My Wallet.
  Early release requests must be submitted within the Seller Centre.

FAQ:
  Q: I don't have MFi authorization. Can I still appeal?
  A: Yes. Remove "MFi" and "iPhone" from listings, then submit
     a "Product Modification Appeal." Processing: 3-5 business days.

  Q: What if I miss the deadline?
  A: Suspension becomes permanent. New account possible after 180 days.

